\section{Errors, warnings and messages}{

Every error, warning and message of kits has a class, so it can be caught by class, for example
\code{tryCatch(kits_convert(s, link), kits_error_scale = function(e) ...)}.
All errors also have the class \code{kits_error}, all warnings \code{kits_warning}, all messages \code{kits_message}.
\itemize{
\item \code{kits_error_input}: a wrong argument (type, length, missing column, unknown option).
\item \code{kits_error_data}: a problem in the data (row names, ids, scores that are not whole numbers, score gaps,
item patterns that form separate groups with no common items).
\item \code{kits_error_items}: a problem in the item parameters or common items (missing parameters, too few common items or anchors).
\item \code{kits_error_scale}: scales that do not match (a link applied to the wrong scale, a link between two equal scales,
\code{fixed_params} on another scale than \code{scale}, a norm on another scale than the scores,
tables of different scales stacked by \code{rbind()} or \code{bind_rows()}).
\item \code{kits_error_fit}: a model that cannot be fitted (nothing to calibrate, too few points kept, no wave fitted).
\item \code{kits_warning_convergence}: an optimizer that stopped before converging (the norms).
\item \code{kits_warning_scale}: a conversion or link to check (scale not recorded, points negatively related,
no linking error because all points belong to one item, a domain without kept anchors,
a kits table stacked with a plain data.frame).
\item \code{kits_warning_norms}: a norm to check (coefficients at their limits, a large delta).
\item \code{kits_warning_data}: data left out of a comparison (items with different scores in the two groups of \code{\link[=kits_dif]{kits_dif()}}).
\item \code{kits_warning_anchors}: anchors to use with care (\code{\link[=kits_anchors]{kits_anchors()}} with \code{key = "gsed2510"}, another D metric).
\item \code{kits_message_data}: data dropped or worth knowing (empty rows or items, items not drawn, items in one DIF group only).
\item \code{kits_message_scale}: scores that are not on the D scale given to the norm functions, a scale labelled
"scale 1" by default, links that share kept items, and a \code{\link[=kits_convert]{kits_convert()}} that adds no \code{se_link} because a link
of the chain (in this call or an earlier one) has no bootstrap draws.
\item \code{kits_message_fit}: items or waves left out of a fit.
}

Messages and errors give counts, not person ids; set \code{options(kits.show_ids = TRUE)} to show the ids.

To cite kits, see \code{citation("kits")}; please cite the methods below with it.
